[38.264, "o", "The **Google BigQuery Managed MCP Server** (`urn:ai:google.com:mcp:bigquery`) is the right tool. It executes SQL queries, inspects schemas, and dry-runs/cost-estimates queries on BigQuery \u2014 a 100GB dataset is well within its (and BigQuery's) scale.\r\n\r\nIt's Tier 3, requiring GCP auth, and you're not authenticated yet:\r\n- Onboard with: `gcloud auth application-default login`\r\n- Free tier: 1TB query processing / 10GB storage monthly\r\n\r\nWant to allow using this service? If so, I'll record the decision and you can run the auth command above. (Fallback without auth: the no-auth `bigquery-guidelines` skill for query optimization.)\r\n"]
[39.591, "o", "\u001b[?2004hdeveloper@workstation:~/ard-project$ "]
