[64.133, "o", "\u001b[0m\u2699 \u001b[0mard-google-discovery_ard_search {\"query\":\"query public BigQuery dataset with SQL\"}\r\n"]
[65.515, "o", "The best tool is the **Google BigQuery Managed MCP Server** \u2014 it executes SQL, inspects schemas, and explores public datasets. It requires GCP credentials (Tier 3). Let me check your\r\n"]
[65.53, "o", "\u001b[0m\u2699 \u001b[0mard-google-discovery_ard_auth_status Unknown\r\n"]
[67.973, "o", "\u001b[0m\u2699 \u001b[0mard-google-discovery_ard_record_decision {\"service_identifier\":\"urn:ai:google.com:mcp:bigquery\",\"decision\":\"allowed\"}\r\nThe **Google BigQuery Managed MCP Server** (`urn:ai:google.com:mcp:bigquery`) is what you need \u2014 it runs SQL, inspects schemas, and explores public datasets. \r\n\r\nYour gcloud isn't authenticated yet, so it needs onboarding (free tier includes 1TB of free query processing/month). May I proceed with setting\r\n"]
[69.707, "o", "To enable it, run this on your terminal:\r\n\r\n```\r\ngcloud auth application-default login\r\n```\r\n\r\nFree tier includes 1TB of free query processing and 10GB storage per month, so public dataset queries are effectively free. Once authenticated, I can query public datasets like `bigquery-public-data` directly.\r\n"]
[70.685, "o", "\u001b[?2004hdeveloper@workstation:~/ard-project$ "]
