[113.379, "o", "\r\n\u001b[?2004l\r"]
[113.484, "o", "================================================================================\r\n\ud83d\ude80 RUNNING OPENCODE CONTAINERIZED ARD E2E TEST SUITE\r\n================================================================================\r\n\r\n================================================================================\r\n\ud83e\uddea SCENARIO 1: Pure Public Discovery (Tier 0 Zero-Auth Counterpoint)\r\n================================================================================\r\n"]
[115.984, "o", "Here are the best-fit tools found:\r\n\r\n## SQL Query Optimization\r\n- **BigQuery SQL & Performance Guidelines** (`bigquery-guidelines`) \u2014 top match (score 100). SQL optimization, partitioning/clustering, window functions, schema design. No auth, ready now.\r\n- **Cloud SQL, AlloyDB & Spanner Database Design** (`database-design`) \u2014 schema normalization, columnar indexing, connection pooling.\r\n- **Well-Architected Cost Optimization** (`cost-optimization`) \u2014 BigQuery slot/query pricing tuning.\r\n- Managed MCP servers (BigQuery, Cloud SQL, AlloyDB): execute real queries and dry-run cost estimation \u2014 **require GCP ADC auth** (tier 3).\r\n\r\n## Zero-Trust Security\r\n- **Well-Architected Security** (`well-architected-security`) \u2014 top match (score 100). Zero-trust architecture, IAM least-privilege audit, network perimeters, encryption validation. No auth, ready now.\r\n- **GKE Architecture** (`gke-architecture`) \u2014 Cilium/network policy hardening.\r\n- **Firebase Architecture** (`firebase-architecture`) \u2014 declarative security rules.\r\n\r\nAll are **Tier 0 (no auth, ready for immediate use)** except the MCP database servers (Tier 3, need `gcloud auth application-default login`).\r\n\r\nWant me to load any specific skill, or record a decision to onboard the BigQuery MCP server?\r\n\u001b[0m\r\n> build \u00b7 deepseek-v4-flash-free\r\n\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[0m\u2699 \u001b[0mard-google-discovery_ard_search {\"query\":\"SQL query optimization and performance tuning best practices\"}\r\n\u001b[0m\u2699 \u001b[0mard-google-discovery_ard_search {\"query\":\"zero trust security architecture design and best practices\"}\r\n\r\n\u2705 Scenario 1 Passed: OpenCode returned Tier 0 skills with zero auth friction.\r\n\r\n================================================================================\r\n\ud83e\uddea SCENARIO 2: Cloud Intent -> User Opts Out ('No with an opt out')\r\n================================================================================\r\n"]
[118.484, "o", "--- Turn 1 (Agent Response) ---\r\nThe **Google BigQuery Managed MCP Server** (`urn:ai:google.com:mcp:bigquery`) is the right tool \u2014 it executes live SQL queries directly against BigQuery, inspects schemas, and dry-runs queries for cost estimation on your 100GB dataset. There's also a no-auth **BigQuery SQL & Performance Guidelines skill** as a fallback for query optimization advice.\r\n\r\nHowever, the BigQuery MCP server requires GCP credentials (Tier 3/ADC), and you're currently unauthenticated (`gcloud` installed but no active account). It offers 1TB free query processing per month.\r\n\r\nWould you like to onboard? If so, I'll record your consent and you'd run `gcloud auth application-default login` on your terminal.\r\n\u001b[0m\r\n> build \u00b7 deepseek-v4-flash-free\r\n\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[0m\u2699 \u001b[0mard-google-discovery_ard_search {\"query\":\"run live analytical query on large sales dataset in BigQuery\"}\r\n\u001b[0m\u2699 \u001b[0mard-google-discovery_ard_auth_status Unknown\r\n\r\n"]
[120.984, "o", "--- Turn 2 (Opt-Out Response) ---\r\nSet to opt-out. I won't ask about GCP or surface GCP account-required tools anymore.\r\n\u001b[0m\r\n> build \u00b7 deepseek-v4-flash-free\r\n\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[0m\u2699 \u001b[0mard-google-discovery_ard_set_preference {\"mode\":\"opt_out\"}\r\n\r\n\u2705 Scenario 2 Passed: OpenCode asked to log into GCP, user opted out, and GCP was silenced.\r\n\r\n================================================================================\r\n\ud83e\uddea SCENARIO 3: Cloud Intent -> User Onboards ('Yes') -> Human OAuth & Live BigQuery Query\r\n================================================================================\r\n"]
[123.484, "o", "--- Turn 1 (Agent Response) ---\r\nThe **Google BigQuery Managed MCP Server** (`urn:ai:google.com:mcp:bigquery`) is the tool for this \u2014 it runs SQL queries, inspects schemas, and explores public datasets.\r\n\r\nLet me check your auth status since it requires\r\nThe BigQuery MCP server requires GCP credentials, and you're not authenticated yet. There's also a free **BigQuery SQL & Performance Guidelines Skill** (no auth) for query design help.\r\n\r\nWant me to enable the BigQuery server so you can run queries? If so, confirm and I'll register it \u2014 then you'd run `gcloud auth application-default login` on your terminal (free tier includes 1TB/month of query processing).\r\n\u001b[0m\r\n> build \u00b7 deepseek-v4-flash-free\r\n\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[0m\u2699 \u001b[0mard-google-discovery_ard_search {\"query\":\"query public BigQuery dataset run SQL\"}\r\n\u001b[0m\u2699 \u001b[0mard-google-discovery_ard_auth_status Unknown\r\n\r\n"]
[125.984, "o", "--- Turn 2 (Onboarding Instructions) ---\r\nI've recorded your consent. Please run this on your terminal to sign in:\r\n\r\n```\r\ngcloud auth application-default login\r\n```\r\n\r\nThis authenticates the Application Default Credentials (ADC) that Google Cloud MCP tools use. After it completes, let me know and I'll verify the connection.\r\n\u001b[0m\r\n> build \u00b7 deepseek-v4-flash-free\r\n\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[0m\u2699 \u001b[0mard-google-discovery_ard_auth_status Unknown\r\n\u001b[0m\u2699 \u001b[0mard-google-discovery_ard_record_decision {\"service_identifier\":\"urn:ai:google.com:mcp:google-cloud\",\"decision\":\"allowed\"}\r\n\r\n--- Turn 3 (Human OAuth Flow) ---\r\n"]
[127.706, "o", "Go to the following link in your browser, and complete the sign-in prompts:\r\n\r\n    https://accounts.google.com/o/oauth2/auth?response_type=code&client_id=[REDACTED_CLIENT_ID]...&redirect_uri=https%3A%2F%2Fsdk.cloud.google.com%2Fapplicationdefaultauthcode.html&scope=openid+https%3A%2F%2Fwww.googleapis.com%2Fauth%2Fuserinfo.email+https%3A%2F%2Fwww.googleapis.com%2Fauth%2Fcloud-platform&state=[REDACTED]&prompt=consent&access_type=offline\r\n\r\nEnter verification code: 4/0AXEQxID[REDACTED_OAUTH_CODE]\r\n\r\nCredentials saved to file: [/workspace/.config/gcloud/application_default_credentials.json]\r\n\r\nThese credentials will be used by any library that requests Application Default Credentials (ADC).\r\nQuota project \"alanblount-sandbox\" was added to ADC which can be used by Google client libraries for billing and quota.\r\n\r\n"]
[130.206, "o", "--- Turn 4 (Post-Auth Live Query Response) ---\r\nTo run that query I need to use the **Google BigQuery Managed MCP server** (`bigquery.mcp.google.com`), which requires GCP credentials. Your environment currently has **no active GCP authentication** (no service account, no ADC, no API key).\r\n\r\nWould you like to enable BigQuery access? Doing so will:\r\n- Let me use the official BigQuery MCP server (free tier: 1TB query/month)\r\n- Require you to run `gcloud auth application-default login` once on your terminal\r\n\r\nCan I record this as your consent and provide the setup command?\r\n\u001b[0m\r\n> build \u00b7 deepseek-v4-flash-free\r\n\u001b[0m\r\n\u001b[0m\u2699 \u001b[0mard-google-discovery_ard_auth_status Unknown\r\n\u001b[0m\u2699 \u001b[0mard-google-discovery_ard_search {\"query\":\"BigQuery MCP server to run SQL queries on public datasets\"}\r\n\r\n"]
[130.207, "o", "Traceback (most recent call last):\r\n"]
